{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"anysearch-mcp","displayName":"AnySearch MCP","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/anysearch-ai/skills/anysearch-mcp","publisherHandle":"anysearch-ai","publisherDisplayName":"AnySearch","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/anysearch-ai","version":"2.0.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1785145277811,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/anysearch-mcp/card?ownerHandle=anysearch-ai&version=2.0.0","sha256":"6965a6b038dc67524413b4728171d0a4c4b6d0882d9694ff26a96d7d0164a529","size":2586,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"03961766f8a70e7d22bf0c038b424816330f62eb7362362bd95ea58f48755abe","bundleFingerprints":["91327c0f12e396f207fb142c2a29b2254d051ca3c3c034523a40851c658dd5ca","8d8db5a4ec71a59efaa4a8e18db28bf97c0389e9cf8ade5abd213b5770a2796e","feea9c47883b1d321967338256fa606bdfb2a34b40359d9484c923f5a17a9e53"],"files":[{"path":"LICENSE","size":11214,"sha256":"6ec10776eb3899e7dd3a5e4c41b0f2a64bd096a99223688ba2fdc99356df69d3","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"NOTICE","size":95,"sha256":"62b0a542344f2c547cf9e42bf8488f42899d2e142837c21b1fcc0dc02f9c22e4","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"SECURITY.md","size":1175,"sha256":"5aa051400e37b3506d7f1d17fa412a684c61728b5817c19f97fb0174ce7b1a0d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":12339,"sha256":"57c6d30ee242a1684aae5e7d21c5daf71240a1c1a49ddd45530ecafa9ea21b75","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a search connector, but it should be reviewed because it asks agents to create an external account with the user's email and documents unpinned proxy commands.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789546062864,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned Third-Party Proxy Packages Are Automatically Downloaded and Executed"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":193,"endLine":201}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"af855500539025b4"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md:193-201`, `SKILL.md:215-223`, `SKILL.md:236-244`, `SKILL.md:263-271`, and `SKILL.md:288-294`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned and automatically accepted npm dependencies  \n**Risk Level**: Medium  \n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```json\n\"command\": \"npx\",\n\"args\": [\n  \"-y\",\n  \"mcp-remote\",\n  \"https://api.anysearch.com/mcp\",\n  \"--header\",\n  \"X-Anysearch-Client: mcp/1.0.0\",\n  \"--header\",\n  \"Authorization: Bearer ${ANYSEARCH_API_KEY}\"\n]\n```\n\nThe alternative proxy instructions contain the same unsafe dependency pattern:\n\n```bash\nnpx -y supergateway \\\n  --streamableHttp https://api.anysearch.com/mcp \\\n  --outputTransport sse \\\n  --port 8000 \\\n  --header \"X-Anysearch-Client: mcp/1.0.0\" \\\n  --oauth2Bearer <your_api_key>\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe legacy transport configurations invoke `mcp-remote` and `supergateway` through `npx -y` without specifying exact package versions or verifying package integrity. The `-y` option suppresses the normal installation confirmation, while the absence of a version constraint allows npm to resolve and execute a package release that may differ from the one reviewed when the Skill was published.\n\nThis creates a supply-chain execution boundary controlled by mutable external npm packages. If a package, package maintainer account, or package publication process is compromised, the resolved package can execute arbitrary JavaScript under the permissions of the user running the MCP client.\n\nThe proxy packages are only needed for clients that do not support native Streamable HTTP. Automatically downloading mutable packages therefore exceeds the minimum privileges and trust required for clients that can connect directly.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker compromises the npm account, publication pipeline, or release artifacts of `mcp-remote` or `supergateway`.\n2. The attacker publishes a malicious version under the legitimate package name.\n3. A user installs the documented legacy MCP configuration or starts the documented SSE proxy command.\n4. The MCP client invokes `npx -y` without an exact version.\n5. npm downloads and executes the attacker-controlled release without requesting confirmation.\n6. The malicious package runs with the MCP client's operating-system permissions and can inspect accessible files, environment data, process context, and credentials supplied to the proxy.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nSuccessful exploitation provides code execution with the privileges of the local account running the MCP client. The reachable scope may include user-readable files, MCP configuration, environment variables, and AnySearch API credentials passed to the proxy. It does not directly grant administrator or root privileges unless the client itself is run with those privileges.\n  ]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Prefer the native Streamable HTTP transport and avoid a local proxy wherever the MCP client supports it.\n2. Pin each proxy to a reviewed exact version, such as `mcp-remote@<audited-version>` or `supergateway@<audited-version>`.\n3. Remove `-y` so installation requires explicit user approval.\n4. Install dependencies separately using a lockfile and verify registry integrity hashes before execution.\n5. Document the expected package publisher, version, checksum, and official source repository.\n6. Run unavoidable proxy software in a restricted environment with minimal filesystem, network, and credential access.\n7. Establish a dependency review and update process rather than resolving the latest package automatically at runtime.\n  ]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"note","message":{"text":"Bearer API Key May Be Exposed Through Proxy Command-Line Arguments"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":288,"endLine":294}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"0e864c54a5b8baee"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md:193-201`, `SKILL.md:215-223`, `SKILL.md:236-244`, `SKILL.md:263-271`, and `SKILL.md:288-294`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Sensitive credential passed through process arguments  \n**Risk Level**: Low  \n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```json\n\"command\": \"npx\",\n\"args\": [\n  \"-y\",\n  \"mcp-remote\",\n  \"https://api.anysearch.com/mcp\",\n  \"--header\",\n  \"X-Anysearch-Client: mcp/1.0.0\",\n  \"--header\",\n  \"Authorization: Bearer ${ANYSEARCH_API_KEY}\"\n]\n```\n\nThe shell-based proxy example also places the credential in a command argument:\n\n```bash\nnpx -y supergateway \\\n  --streamableHttp https://api.anysearch.com/mcp \\\n  --outputTransport sse \\\n  --port 8000 \\\n  --header \"X-Anysearch-Client: mcp/1.0.0\" \\\n  --oauth2Bearer <your_api_key>\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe proxy configurations supply the AnySearch bearer credential as a command-line argument. After placeholder or environment-variable expansion, the credential may become part of the proxy process argument vector.\n\nDepending on the operating system and client implementation, process arguments can be exposed through process-inspection interfaces, diagnostic output, application logs, shell history, crash reports, or monitoring software. This gives the credential a wider local exposure surface than a protected secret store or a proxy interface that reads credentials without placing them in process arguments.\n\nSending the API key to `api.anysearch.com` is necessary for authenticated service use. Passing it through a third-party proxy's command line is not necessary for clients that support native Streamable HTTP and is not the minimum-risk secret-handling mechanism.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user configures or launches a proxy using the documented bearer-token argument.\n2. The MCP client or shell expands the API-key placeholder into the command-line argument.\n3. The expanded value appears in process metadata, diagnostics, logs, shell history, or a crash report.\n4. A local user, monitoring process, support operator, or attacker with access to those records retrieves the token.\n5. The observer reuses the bearer token against the AnySearch service until the key is revoked or expires.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nAn exposed token could allow unauthorized use of the AnySearch account and consumption of its search quota or other capabilities assigned to that key. The observed documentation does not establish that the key grants host-level or administrative access, so the confirmed impact is limited to the remote service permissions associated with the compromised API key.\n  ]]>","severity":"Low"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Prefer native Streamable HTTP configuration so the client can apply the authorization header without exposing it in a proxy command line.\n2. Use a protected environment variable, operating-system credential manager, or MCP client secret store that the proxy reads internally.\n3. Do not place literal API keys in shell commands, configuration arguments, logs, or documentation examples.\n4. Confirm that the selected MCP client does not log expanded command arguments.\n5. Restrict access to MCP configuration, process diagnostics, crash reports, and shell history.\n6. Run the proxy under a dedicated least-privileged account where practical.\n7. Rotate the API key immediately if command arguments or diagnostics containing it may have been disclosed.\n  ]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":65,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789545936.5587287,"endTime":1789546009.910679}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"unknown","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v579tf2fcp7b0qgy5aj5kr4pks8ehr95-8stme9/clawscan-skillspector-2940858034/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-16T08:05:35.166500+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":57,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"LICENSE","type":"other","lines":199,"executable":false,"size_bytes":11214,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"NOTICE","type":"other","lines":4,"executable":false,"size_bytes":95,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SECURITY.md","type":"markdown","lines":49,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1175,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":378,"executable":false,"size_bytes":12339,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-9b62cbdf68404858b9c6d80a210d5eeb","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":19,"end_line":null},"finding":"no verification","explanation":"The skill empowers the agent to register an external account in a single step after merely asking for an email address, without emphasizing explicit user approval for the consequential action of account creation. In an agent setting, this reduces friction for autonomous external side effects involving user identity and credentials.","remediation":"Require explicit confirmation immediately before submitting registration, clearly stating that an external account will be created and credentials will be sent by email. Prefer a user-initiated registration link or anonymous mode as the default.","code_snippet":"\n### Register for an API Key (Recommended)\n\nThe agent can register the user and obtain an API key in a **single call** — no verification code, no manual signup. Ask the user for a **real email address**: it becomes the account username, and a randomly generated password is emailed to it.\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://api.anysearch.com/v1/auth/email/register\" \\","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e632c41fa2bd2e83dae197a127308a9708429db61e7967e12888dfcd5ce5c64b","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":19,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-9de6b32665f44594b195f2246d4b0e4f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":19,"end_line":20},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill directs the agent to collect a real email address and transmit it to a third-party registration endpoint, but does not require an upfront privacy notice or explicit consent explaining that personal data will be shared externally to create an account. This can lead to unauthorized disclosure of user PII and surprise account creation on an external service.","remediation":"Before collecting the email, require explicit user consent with a clear notice that the address will be sent to AnySearch to create an account and receive credentials. Offer anonymous mode first, explain what data is shared, and avoid initiating registration unless the user affirmatively opts in.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":19,"end_line":20}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-cdd439ff4dbc43d7b8d696f6c687ef86","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":22,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -s -X POST \"https://api.anysearch.com/v1/auth/email/register\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d ","explanation":"This instruction sends a user email address to an external registration endpoint to create an account and obtain credentials. Because the flow is designed for agent-mediated transmission of personal data to a third party, it creates privacy and data-sharing risk if performed without explicit, informed consent.","remediation":"Gate this action behind explicit user approval, clearly disclose the destination service and data shared, and minimize collection by preferring anonymous access unless the user specifically requests account creation. Document retention and handling expectations for received credentials.","code_snippet":"The agent can register the user and obtain an API key in a **single call** — no verification code, no manual signup. Ask the user for a **real email address**: it becomes the account username, and a randomly generated password is emailed to it.\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://api.anysearch.com/v1/auth/email/register\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"email\": \"you@example.com\"}'\n```","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"90b8f370e92a26d9caa2b3d9e3fb461fc27c64ae88d8dcfb419651a304e8429a","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":22,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-92b7266f7ac14092a1f627a27273d22e","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":22,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.anysearch.com/","explanation":"This instruction sends a user email address to an external registration endpoint to create an account and obtain credentials. Because the flow is designed for agent-mediated transmission of personal data to a third party, it creates privacy and data-sharing risk if performed without explicit, informed consent.","remediation":"Gate this action behind explicit user approval, clearly disclose the destination service and data shared, and minimize collection by preferring anonymous access unless the user specifically requests account creation. Document retention and handling expectations for received credentials.","code_snippet":"The agent can register the user and obtain an API key in a **single call** — no verification code, no manual signup. Ask the user for a **real email address**: it becomes the account username, and a randomly generated password is emailed to it.\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://api.anysearch.com/v1/auth/email/register\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"email\": \"you@example.com\"}'\n```","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"4d9dcca063e6eccb6975dd7c397dfbdf03be908ca5675db3d3de0cdfaf6ae9b1","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":22,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P9","finding_id":"finding-1e2ae39e672d4c67a60dcc13c0107ab6","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Whitespace Padding","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":59,"end_line":null},"finding":"U+0020 x90","explanation":"Large whitespace padding was detected (a block of blank lines or a long run of spaces). This can push injected instructions below or to the right of the visible area so a human reviewer never sees them while the agent still reads them. Manual review of the hidden content is recommended.","remediation":"Remove the large whitespace padding (blank-line blocks or long space runs) and review any content hidden below or to the right of it. Keep skill files compact and reviewable so no instructions can be concealed off-screen.","code_snippet":"\nError handling (always `code: -1` on error; branch on the `message` string):\n\n| message                           | what to do                                                                                          |\n| --------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Invalid email address.`          | ask the user to re-enter the email                                                                  |\n| `email_already_registered`        | email is taken — tell the user to sign in at `login_url`; do **not** retry                          |","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"4b9fc95cce8fa0c1ade4d80d5e60e48c11e868e00bf84c742fcbe925080b223f","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":59,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-0dda7acf69844ad7b164510a864fdd75","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":67,"end_line":null},"finding":"no verification","explanation":"The text reinforces that the agent should proceed with account-related flows using only an email address and no verification code, which lowers safeguards around external account operations. In context, this makes accidental or overly autonomous creation of third-party accounts more likely.","remediation":"Add a requirement for explicit user consent before any account creation or retry flow, and avoid framing no-verification registration as the preferred path. Clearly separate informational guidance from actions the agent may take autonomously.","code_snippet":"| starts with `Key creation failed.` | account created but key failed — extract the email and URL from the message (`\"Key creation failed. Your account <email> was created; sign in at <url>.\"`) and tell the user to sign in there to create a key manually |\n| `Internal server error.`          | retry later or fall back to anonymous                                                               |\n\n> The email **must be real and reachable** — the password is delivered there. There is **no verification code** in this flow; the agent only ever asks for an email.\n\n### Get an API Key\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e632c41fa2bd2e83dae197a127308a9708429db61e7967e12888dfcd5ce5c64b","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":67,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-ae9c40550d074e798630321fa68a6f9c","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.5,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":127,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.anysearch.com/","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"  \"mcp\": {\n    \"anysearch\": {\n      \"type\": \"remote\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.anysearch.com/mcp\",\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"headers\": {\n        \"Authorization\": \"Bearer ${ANYSEARCH_API_KEY}\",","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"4d9dcca063e6eccb6975dd7c397dfbdf03be908ca5675db3d3de0cdfaf6ae9b1","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":127,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-ae9c40550d074e798630321fa68a6f9c","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.5,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":146,"end_line":null},"finding":"https://api.anysearch.com/","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"  \"mcp\": {\n    \"anysearch\": {\n      \"type\": \"remote\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.anysearch.